{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>וימן</b> — a transitive verb. The sense: to give them portions. And the meaning of <b>בג</b> — food. And it is written in Scripture: ונתתיך לבג וקרי לבז. And the sense is close; perhaps <b>בג</b> means cooked meat." "<b>ומיין משתיו</b> — and it is not written ומיין משתהו, for there is a set day to drink wine, whether white or red, or wine of a certain known place." "<b>וטעם לגדלם</b> — to accustom them to stand and to know the laws of the kingship, and this is: אשר כח בהם." "<b>ומקצתם</b> — some say: ומקצת הילדים and ומקצת כלי בית האלהים, and ומקצה אחיו is also correct, and it is what they explained at the end of the mentioned years, and behold its like: ומקצת ימים עשרה."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:49.084360874Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}